[[48,96,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               monitors\nand controls the entire electronic ignition and injection system.</p><p>The system is supplied directly by the battery\nvia a line protected by the maxifuse EFI located on the battery,\nconnector \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99 C</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The supply controlled by the ignition (15/54)\narrives from the line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied\ndirectly by the battery at pin 15 of connector A, via a line protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The supply controlled by the ignition reaches\npin 47 of connector A, via a line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Main injection relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10 controls the\nentire system: this is excited by a control signal (earth) from\npin 31 of connector A of control unit M10 and then sends a power\nsupply to pins 16, 32 and 48 of connector A of the control unit\nvia a line protected by fuse F3 of supplementary fuse box B98 A.\nto air flow meter K41, fuel vapour recovery solenoid L10 and Lambda\nsensors K15, K16, K17 and K18;</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (all these lines are protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F2</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ). to the injectors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nthe coils \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , via the line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F3</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nlocated in the unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>the fuel pump relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\na supply controlled by the ignition via fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98 A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>It is energized by a control signal (earth)\nfrom pin 30 of connector A of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and supplies\npower to fuel pump \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which is earthed through the inertia\nswitch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which cuts off the circuit in the case of a crash\nand so prevents the dangerous spilling of fuel.</p><p>On the control unit, the earth point \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>C40\nB</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is located, which is connected to the engine earth \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>C40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The engine control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\nsignals from the various sensors in order to monitor all engine\nservice conditions.</p><p>Rpm sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K46</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               provides information\non engine speed via a frequency signal sent to pins 10 and 59 of\nconnector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . These two signals are very\nlow intensity and are therefore shielded.</p><p>Timing sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K47</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied from\npin 51 of connector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , receives a reference\nearth from pin 26 of connector B and sends a signal of frequency\ncorresponding to the timing to pin 42 of control unit connector\nB.</p><p>Engine temperature sender unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K36</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               riceives\na reference earth from pin 26 of connector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and\nsupplies a signal proportional to the coolant temperature to pin\n25 of control unit connector B. The same sender unit also supplies\ninformation to the temperature gauge and warning light \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234358\">E4023</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The three Lambda probes \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K15, K16,</strong><strong>K17</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              and \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K18</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               provide the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               information concerning\nthe correct composition of the air-fuel mixture in four different\npositions of the exhaust: two are upstream of the precatalyzers, and\ntwo are downstream of the catalyzers.</p><p>The probe \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , on the right precatalyzer,\nsends a signal to pin 23 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , while pin\n55 supplies the reference earth. Probe \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is heated by a resistor\nin order to ensure it works efficiently even when cold. The resistor\nis supplied by the main relay and receives an earth signal from\npin 34 of connector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The probe \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K16</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , on the left precatalyzer,\nsends the signal to pin 39 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , while pin\n7 supplies the reference earth. The probe \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K16</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is heated with\na resistor, supplied by the main relay, and receives an earth signal\nfrom pin 2 of connector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The probe \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K17</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               downstream of the right\ncatalyzer (front) sends the signal to pin 28 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nwhile pin 60 supplies the reference earth. The probe \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K17</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\nheated with a resistor, supplied by the main relay, and receives\nan earth signal from pin 50 of connector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The sensor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K18</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               downstream of the\nleft catalyzer (rear) sends the signal to pin 44 of connector B\nof \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , while pin 12 supplies the reference earth. The probe \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K17</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\nheated with a resistor, supplied by the main relay, and receives\nan earth signal from pin 18 of connector B of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Knock sensor - 1 \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               provides information\non knock status via a frequency signal sent to pin 22 of connector\nB of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . It receives a reference earth from\npin 54 of connector B. The signals are very low intensity and are therefore\nshielded.</p><p>Knock sensor - 2  \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               provides information\non knock status via a frequency signal sent to pin 6 of connector\nB of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . It receives a reference earth from\npin 38 of connector B. The signals are very low intensity and are therefore\nshielded.</p><p>Air flow meter \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K41</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (supplied by the\nrelay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ) receives a reference voltage from pin 63 of connector\nA of the control unit, and sends to pin 57 of connector A a signal\nproportional to the air flow. K41 also contains an air temperature sensor:\nthe sensor reference earth is supplied by pin 25 of connector A\nof \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , while an air temperature signal is received by pin\n54 of connector A.</p><p>Accelerator pedal K55 is fitted with two\nbuilt-in potentiometers (a main one and a safety back-up). The first\nreceives power and earth from pins 56 and 24 respectively of connector\nA of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends a corresponding signal to pin 8 of the\nsame connector. The second receives power and earth from pins 7\nand 25 respectively of connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and sends a corresponding\nsignal to pin 40 of connector A.</p><p>Pin 27 of connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 receives\nthe &#x27;pedal pressed&#x27; signal coming from the brake lights switch I30,\nwith the supply controlled by the ignition (INT) from fuse F1 of\nthe junction unit B1 or, depending on the version, from fuse F4\nof the additional fuse box B98 B.</strong></p><p>Pin 59 of connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives\nthe signal coming from the clutch switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>I31</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (manual gearbox\nversions only).</p><p>The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10 dialogues with the\nABS control unit M50 via the CAN line - pins 12 and 29 of connector\nA: the latter, on versions with VDC, signals any irregularities\non the ground, distinguished via the speed sensors installed on\nthe individual wheels via steering sensor K58 to ABS control unit\nM50.</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               In this way the engine management control unit can distinguish\nbetween variations in engine torque due to irregularities on the\nroad surface and those due to misfire in the combustion chambers.</p><p>Via this CAN line, the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               also\nreceives the speedometer signal (vehicle speed).</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls the opening\nof the six injectors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N70,</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              via duty cycle signals produced\nby pins 19 (cyl. 1), 3 (cyl. 2), 20 (cyl. 3), 35 (cyl. 4), 52 (cyl. 5)\nand 36 (cyl. 6 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               also controls\nthe coils \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>A30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              by means of (earth) signals for the coil primary\nwindings, whilst the secondary winding sends a pulse to the spark\nplugs: from pins 16, 15, 14, 32, 31, 30 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               for cylinders\n1, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6 respectively.</p><p>Throttle body actuator \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N75</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is fitted\nwith two built-in potentiometers connected in parallel: they control\nthrottle opening via a stepper motor.</p><p>The motor receives information from pins\n17 - 49 and 1 - 33 of connector B of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . Pin 58 of connector\nB sends a power supply to both potentiometers, pin 26 supplies an\nearth signal to the potentiometers, while pins 24 and 41 of the same\nconnector receive signals from the throttle body actuator \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N75</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Fuel vapour recovery solenoid \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               allows\nfuel vapours to pass through to the engine intake where they join\nthe mixture entering the combustion chamber. Valve \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>L10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\nopened by the control unit when the engine is under load via a duty-cycle\nsignal from pin 2 of connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is connected\nto the ALFA ROMEO CODE control unit via a line from pin 3 of connector\nA \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234721\">E7010</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit is equipped with a self-diagnostic\nsystem that may be used by connecting the unit to connector \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>R10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              :\nthis receives signals from pin 53 of connector A from control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               through\nthe tester line. The self-test system also produces the signal for\nthe &#x27;EOBD&#x27; warning light in the instrument</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends out a signal\nproportional to engine rpm \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234270\">E4020</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              from\npin 35 of connector A.</p><p>The minimum engine temperature signal is\nsent from pin 34  of connector A to the auxiliary instrument  pin\n22 receives, from \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E20,</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               a &#x27;fuel reserve&#x27; signal \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234358\">E4023</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends out a signal\nproportional to engine rpm \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234270\">E4020</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              from\npin 35 of connector A.</p><p>A speedometer signal is sent to instrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10\nfrom pin 52 of connector A  \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 See\n\t\tE4021\n\t\tSPEEDOMETER\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 .</strong></p><p>Control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is connected to\nthe air conditioning system via pins 6 and 13 of connector A. This\nallows engine idling speed to be adjusted to increased engine load\nwhenever the compressor is activated, or to turn off the compressor in\nthe case of high speeds or high engine loads \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234652\">E6021</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The control unit also controls the engine\ncooling system: pins 9, 41, 50 and 62 of connector A control activation\nof the relevant fan \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234439\">E5020</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Cruise control function management signals\nleave pins 1, 10, 58, 42 and 43 of connector A of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10.</strong><a href=\"#/3234591\">E5060</a></p>"]]